        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): use truncateUtf16Safe for CDP DOM text snapshot truncation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nCDP DOM text snapshots in `extensions/browser/src/browser/cdp.ts` use `.trim().slice(0, 101)` on live DOM text content. A slice boundary that lands in the middle of a surrogate pair (common with emoji and CJK characters in web pages) produces U+FFFD replacement characters.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace the `.slice(0, 101)` call with `truncateUtf16Safe()`. `truncateUtf16Safe` is already imported at line 8 of this file but was not used at this call site.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Code change (1 line, import already in place)\n\n```diff\n- text: String(el.textContent || \"\").replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim().slice(0, 101),\n+ text: truncateUtf16Safe(String(el.textContent || \"\").replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim(), 101),\n```\n\n### Follows established pattern\n\nPart of the UTF-16 safety sweep following Alix-007 (#101311), wangmiao (#101421), and ly85206559 (#101029).\n\n## Issue\n\nN/A\n\n---\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
